Based on your answers, your organisation is likely an **essential entity** under NIS2. This means, among other things:

- **Duty of care**: appropriate and proportionate cybersecurity risk-management measures (Art. 21 NIS2);
- **Reporting obligation**: report significant incidents to the CSIRT or competent authority (Art. 23 NIS2);
- **Management accountability**: management bodies approve the measures and follow training (Art. 20 NIS2);
- **Registration obligation** with the competent authority (Art. 3(4) and Art. 27 NIS2);
- **Proactive supervision** (ex ante) by the supervisory authority (Art. 32 NIS2).

In the Netherlands, NIS2 is implemented in the [Cyberbeveiligingswet (Cbw)](https://www.digitaleoverheid.nl/overzicht-van-alle-onderwerpen/cybersecurity/kaders-voor-cybersecurity/cyberbeveiligingswet/). This outcome is indicative; consult the law and the competent supervisory authority for your sector.

